{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"1898 ps1 CI: Verified-1, but ONLY macos-latest py3.13 (canceled at 21m32s = job timeout, NOT an assertion failure); all 3 Linux jobs + lint/typecheck passed full suite. Hypothesis: ps1's config.repo_root() fires a 'git rev-parse --show-toplevel' subprocess on every REBAR_ROOT-unset reconciler call — cheap on Linux, slow enough on the macOS runner to tip the suite past its timeout. ps2's reconciler_repo_root() fix REMOVES those subprocess calls (Path(__file__).parents[2], no git), so ps2 should be faster on macOS. Awaiting ps2 macOS result to confirm (also an env/timeout-class fault under CONTRIBUTING §6, but the fix addresses the root cause directly)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787130634109169001,"uuid":"f90a081b-5538-4ea5-834d-61b727553b55"}